Rāma clasps jewel to heart and weeps with Lakṣmaṇa --- Rāma tells Sugrīva heart melts like cow for calf at jewel sight --- Rāma recalls wedding jewel from father-in-law and Indra sacrifice gift --- Rāma says jewel restores fathers and beloved to mind --- Rāma begs Hanumān to repeat Sītā words like water on fainting --- Rāma mourns seeing jewel without Vaidehī and fears brief life --- Rāma vows he cannot live a moment without dark-eyed Sītā --- Rāma bids Hanumān take him where his beloved was found --- Rāma pictures moonlike face dimmed by Rākṣasas and asks how she lives through grief
